%!demo
%! ## The name travels with the drawing into whatever the output can hold: a
%! ## DXF file records it, a TikZ picture writes it into a comment.  It never
%! ## affects the geometry.
%!
%! D = draw.Drawing ('bracket');
%! D = D.polyline ([0, 0; 60, 0; 60, 40; 0, 40], true);
%! D.Name
%!
%! ## Renaming an existing drawing is an ordinary assignment, because the name
%! ## is a property and not something fixed at construction.
%! D.Name = 'bracket rev B';
%! D.Name
